    "title": "Eid ul-Fitr 2026 Moon Sighting Date, Timing Highlights: Saudi Arabia, UAE marks Eid today; India to celebrate on March 21",
    "text": "Eid al-Fitr 2026 Moon Sighting Date and Time Highlights: Catch all the live updates here.Eid ul-Fitr 2026 Moon Sighting Date, Timing Highlights Updates: Eid ul-Fitr, also known as Meethi Eid, marks the end of the holy month of Ramadan and is one of the most significant festivals in Islam. This year, Saudi Arabia has officially announced that Eid al-Fitr will be observed on March 20, 2026. The decision follows the non-sighting of the Shawwal crescent moon, completing 30 days of fasting. The kingdom’s moon-sighting committee convened to verify reports, in line with the long-standing Islamic tradition of determining months through lunar observation. Eid ul-Fitr 2026 Date and Time: Know Its History and Significance | When is Eid Al-Fitr In Saudi Arabia, the UAE, and India? The Eid al-Fitr 2026 moon sighting date and time may vary by region, with Saudi Arabia and the UAE usually announcing first, followed by India and Pakistan. Authorities and moon sighting committees will confirm Chand Raat 2026 after sunset observations. Eid is known as the “Festival of Breaking the Fast” because it is observed on the day after the last day of Ramadan. In the Islamic lunar calendar, it falls on the first three days of Shawwal, the tenth month of Hijri. According to the latest Saudi Supreme Court’s official statement, the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia sighted the crescent moon of Shawwal on Thursday, March 19. Eid ul Fitr 2026 Moon Sighting Timing Live Updates: Check Here Hence, Eid al-Fitr in Saudi Arabia and the GCC is being celebrated today, on Friday, 20th March 2026. South Asia, on the other hand, typically commemorates the festival a day later, which means countries like India, Bangladesh, and Pakistan will most likely observe the final day of Roza and sight the moon today, on Friday, March 20, and celebrate Eid on Saturday, March 21. 📣 For more lifestyle news, click here to join our WhatsApp Channel and also follow us on Instagram © IE Online Media Services Pvt LtdThis article was first uploaded on March eighteenth, twenty twenty-six, at zero minutes past eleven in the morning. Tags: Eid Eid al Fitr Eid celebrations Eid Mubarak",
